    "PREAMBLE": "Rambilash Banarsasi Yadav vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30\nJanuary, 2024\nAuthor: Sarang V. Kotwal\nBench: Sarang V. Kotwal\n2024:Bhc-As:5106\n Gokhale 1 of 3 \n In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay\n Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction\n Anticipatory Bail Application No. 177 Of 2023\n Rambilash Banarasi Yadav ..\n Versus\n State of Maharashtra ..\n__ __ __\n Mr. Anup Lahoti for Applicant.\nMs. Mahalakshmi Ganapathy, App for State/Respondent.\n___ _ _\n_\n Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J.\nDate : 30 January 2024 P.C. :\n1.\nThe Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R.No.837 of 2022,\nregistered at Pelhar Police Station, Mira Bhayandar, on 03.10.2022, under section 328 of the Indian Penal Code and under sections 26(2), 4 and 30(2)(e) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred to as 'FSS Act').\n2.\n",
    "facts": "They were carrying banned articles namely 'Gutka'.\nAt about 12.15p.m.\nboth the trucks were intercepted.\nThe search of those trucks was taken.\nHe had ordered some of the goods.\nHe gave the name of the present applicant as the person who was getting those goods from one Arjunsingh for sale in Maharashtra.\n",
